Read a replayed offer's age from the <call> wrapper, and cap the RTP replay filter.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, on top of 0002 (upstream PR #26).

Why, two defects in the PR #26 code, both on the inbound call path:

- PR #26 drops an offer replayed from the offline queue when its `e` attribute (the
  seconds the server held it) is over the caller's 90 s ring timeout, but reads `e`
  off the node CallOffer carries, and whatsmeow hands CallOffer only the <offer>
  child: `e` is on the <call> wrapper, so the check never fired and expired offers
  still rang. onCallRaw now reads the wrapper on the way in and marks the call, and
  onOffer drops a marked one.
- rtpReplayFilter gave every new SSRC a ring before SRTP authentication, so packets
  claiming ever-changing SSRCs grew it without bound. It now tracks at most 64
  streams and passes the rest through unfiltered; SRTP still rejects what is forged.

Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387, round 5.

